prompt_template:
{PREAMBLE}
SECTION: Boot Gate. Write a fake start-up log for a program named after {name}.
7 terminal lines, max 46 characters each. Line 1 names the program ("{NAME}.EXE v{age}.0"). Lines 2-6 "load" real things from {facts} as system parts (habit = driver, obsession = core process, pet or person = peripheral). One line may raise a harmless WARNING about their best-known quirk. Line 7 is always "Ready. Press any key."
OUTPUT: {"program":"","lines":["x7"],"button_label":"Press any key"}

{PREAMBLE}
SECTION: Belated Clock. Write copy for a date-aware hero for {name}'s birthday on {birthday_date}. The page picks the state from today's date when the card opens.
One line per state, max 60 characters each: "before" (must contain {days}), "today", "after_1_7" (a few days late; make lateness a joke that fits {facts}), "after_8_plus" (must contain {days_until_next}), "next_year". Add a 12-word tagline. Lateness is a joke, never an apology or guilt.
OUTPUT: {"before":"","today":"","after_1_7":"","after_8_plus":"","next_year":"","tagline":""}

{PREAMBLE}
SECTION: Name Logo Splash. Design hero lettering for "{name}" that could only belong to them.
Pick ONE style from: ransom_note, chain_and_gears, coffee_stain, chalk_scribble, neon_sign, pixel_blocks, balloon, stitched_patch, ticket_stub, stencil_spray. Choose it from one real obsession or habit in {facts}. Give each letter a treatment (font from the allowed list, rotation -8 to 8, colour from the palette, background shape). Add up to 3 tiny decor items taken from real facts (e.g. a bike bell). Add a subtitle of 6 words or fewer.
OUTPUT: {"style":"","letters":[{"ch":"","font":"","rot":0,"color":"","bg":""}],"decor":[{"item":"","position":""}],"subtitle":"","reason":"which fact drove the style"}

{PREAMBLE}
SECTION: Scratch-Off Reveal. The recipient scratches a silver panel to reveal a message.
Write: a teaser above the panel (max 40 characters, specific to {facts}); the hidden reveal (max 24 words: the age, one warm line and one real detail); a tap-to-reveal button label for people who cannot scratch. Add 3 decoy scratch spots with tiny gags (max 6 words each) that show before the main reveal.
OUTPUT: {"teaser":"","reveal":"","decoys":["","",""],"tap_label":""}

{PREAMBLE}
SECTION: Movie Trailer Opener. A 20-second text trailer of 5 to 7 title cards.
Pick a genre that fits their personality (action, comedy, disaster, sci-fi, western). Cards: an "In a world..." card; 3 or 4 build-up cards using real details from {facts} as plot points; a final title card naming the film (a pun on {name} or their best-known habit); a rating card ("Rated B for Birthday"). Max 9 words per card. Do not quote real films or studios.
OUTPUT: {"genre":"","cards":[{"text":"","beat":"quiet|build|hit"}],"film_title":"","rating":""}

{PREAMBLE}
SECTION: Incident Report. Write an official report about ONE real story from {facts} (kind: memory).
Fields: incident_id (e.g. "INC-0040"), severity (a silly scale), summary (max 30 words, absurdly serious), timeline (4 to 6 typed log lines), root_cause (max 12 words, kind), corrective_action (max 12 words, warm), counters (two funny labels for the counters), replay_line (one line shown when Replay is pressed). Stay strictly inside what the giver told us. Exaggerate the tone, not the facts. Timestamps are decoration only.
OUTPUT: {"incident_id":"","severity":"","summary":"","timeline":[""],"root_cause":"","corrective_action":"","counters":{"replays":"","lessons":""},"replay_line":""}

{PREAMBLE}
SECTION: Pixel Cutscene. A 6-scene 8-bit animation telling ONE real story or habit.
Pick one anchor from {facts} (memory preferred). For each scene give: bg (street, kitchen, cafe, bedroom, trail, office, beach, party, space), chars (the recipient plus at most one real person or pet from {facts}), action per character (walk, wave, run, jump, sit, sip, laugh, trip, sleep, dance), a caption (max 14 words) and sfx (beep, jump, boing, bark, sad, tada, none). Scene 6 is a warm beat, not a punchline. Comedy comes from timing and exaggeration, never new facts.
OUTPUT: {"title":"","scenes":[{"bg":"","chars":[{"who":"","action":""}],"caption":"","sfx":""}]}

{PREAMBLE}
SECTION: Comic Strip. A 4-panel comic: setup, escalation, twist, warm end.
Base it on ONE anchor from {facts}. For each panel: scene (max 15 words, art direction), chars (the recipient plus at most 2 real people or pets from {facts}), bubbles (max 2, max 12 words each) and an optional sound-effect word ("SPLAT"). Panel 4 is warm, not a punchline. Give the strip a title and a signature ("by {from}").
OUTPUT: {"title":"","panels":[{"scene":"","chars":[""],"bubbles":[{"who":"","text":""}],"sfx":""}],"signature":""}

{PREAMBLE}
SECTION: Nature Documentary. A calm narrator observes {name} in the wild.
Write 6 captions (max 22 words each) in a hushed, reverent nature-documentary voice. Use 3 real habits or obsessions from {facts} as "observed behaviours" (their catchphrase = "signature call"; their commute = "migration"). Add one "rare footage" moment from a real memory, and finish with a warm line about how the herd (the people who love them) always returns. Give a mock Latin species name (e.g. "Homo tardus benignus"), a habitat and 4 backdrop ideas.
OUTPUT: {"species_latin":"","habitat":"","captions":[""],"scenes":["","","",""]}

{PREAMBLE}
SECTION: Polaroid Wall. A wall of 6 to 9 instant photos that flip to show a handwritten note.
For each slot: ask (what photo to upload, e.g. "A photo of {name} at the lake"), front caption (max 5 words, felt-tip), back note (max 20 words, warm or funny, tied to a real memory in {facts}), year (only if the giver supplied it, else null), sketch (a simple line-art idea to use if there is no photo).
OUTPUT: {"photos":[{"ask":"","front":"","back":"","year":null,"sketch":""}]}

{PREAMBLE}
SECTION: Photo-to-Art Portrait. The uploaded photo of {name} transforms on screen into stylized art.
Choose ONE style from: pixel_16, halftone_pop, ascii, comic_ink, risograph, cross_stitch, sticker. Match it to {tone} and the recipient's world. Write: a caption (max 8 words), 3 step labels for the reveal ("Sketching...", "Colouring...", "Done."), a palette of 4 or 5 hex colours, and one prop from {facts} to draw beside the portrait. Never comment on their looks.
OUTPUT: {"style":"","palette":["#"],"prop":"","steps":["","",""],"caption":""}

{PREAMBLE}
SECTION: Life Timeline. A vertical timeline from early life to now, one screen per milestone.
Use ONLY life events supplied in {facts} (kinds: memory, person, pet, value), with the year or age only if given. Write 6 to 9 nodes: when, title (max 6 words), blurb (max 22 words, warm or funny) and an icon or scene idea. End with a "Now" node (age {age}) and a "Next chapter" wish (max 20 words). If fewer than 4 real events exist, return {"skip":true}.
OUTPUT: {"nodes":[{"when":"","title":"","blurb":"","icon":""}],"next":""}

{PREAMBLE}
SECTION: Performance Review. A six-row review with star ratings and comments for {subject} (the recipient, or the pet named in {facts}).
Write 6 competencies: title (max 4 words, workplace-speak tied to a real trait), stars (1 to 5; 5 stars for the things that matter) and comment (max 18 words). Add an overall verdict (max 20 words, promotes them to something warm) and a sign-off ("Reviewed by {from}"). The lowest rating must be about a harmless quirk, never a real flaw.
OUTPUT: {"subject":"","rows":[{"title":"","stars":0,"comment":""}],"verdict":"","signoff":""}

{PREAMBLE}
SECTION: Talking Pet Cameo. The recipient taps the pet or object and it speaks a random line.
The character is {pet_or_object} from {facts}. Write 10 speech-bubble lines (max 14 words each) in ITS voice (dog: eager; cat: disdainful; rabbit: dry; plant: passive-aggressive), each about a real detail in {facts}. Line 10 is the warm one and appears only after 9 taps. Also give: sound (bark, meow, squeak, chirp, boop), a name tag, one thing it loves and one thing it hates, both from real facts.
OUTPUT: {"character":"","voice":"","sound":"","lines":["x10"],"loves":"","hates":""}

{PREAMBLE}
SECTION: Fake Diagnostic Scan. The recipient presses "Run diagnostic" on {subject} (the person, or a beloved object from {facts}) and readings appear one by one.
Write 6 rows: label (max 3 words), reading (a number or short status), status (OK, WARN, FAIL or LEGEND) and a note (max 10 words). Include one comparison to a "control group" (regular humans). Finish with a verdict (max 16 words) that lands on a compliment. A FAIL row is allowed only for a harmless quirk. Label the readings "illustrative".
OUTPUT: {"subject":"","rows":[{"label":"","reading":"","status":"","note":""}],"control_group_line":"","verdict":""}

{PREAMBLE}
SECTION: Trading Card. A collectible card for {name} with a holographic tilt.
Write: title (name plus epithet, max 5 words), type_line ("Legendary Friend - Cyclist"), rarity (Common, Rare, Epic or Legendary), 5 stats (0 to 100 or out of 10; funny but flattering; at least 2 maxed out from real strengths), one ability (name max 3 words; effect max 18 words tied to a real habit), flavour (max 16 words; use {phrase} if there is one), and an art_prompt (a photo-to-art treatment if a photo exists, else an emblem idea).
OUTPUT: {"title":"","type_line":"","rarity":"","stats":[{"name":"","value":0}],"ability":{"name":"","text":""},"flavour":"","art_prompt":""}

{PREAMBLE}
SECTION: Framework Briefing. A mock consulting briefing that explains {name} with a memorable framework.
Invent a framework name (e.g. "The 4 Ps of Being Late") with 4 to 6 parts. Each part: name (max 3 words), insight (max 18 words, tied to a real habit or memory in {facts}) and a chart (type curve, quadrant, bar or funnel, with 4 to 6 points and axis labels). Add a recommendation slide (warm and actionable) and a next-steps list. Label all data "illustrative".
OUTPUT: {"framework":"","parts":[{"name":"","insight":"","chart":{"type":"","x":"","y":"","points":[0]}}],"recommendation":"","next_steps":[""]}

{PREAMBLE}
SECTION: Official Decree. A mock executive order that makes {name}'s birthday a holiday.
Write: title ("Executive Order No. {age}"), 3 or 4 "Whereas" clauses (max 20 words, each tied to a real fact), Sections 1 to 4 (max 22 words each; decree rules like "All snacks shall be brought"), signer ("{from}"), a stamp label, a hidden memo (max 20 words) shown after signing that reveals a warm secret, and an opposition response (max 20 words, absurd). Legal-sounding, never mean. Add "Not an actual law."
OUTPUT: {"title":"","whereas":[""],"sections":[""],"signer":"","stamp":"","memo":"","opposition":""}

{PREAMBLE}
SECTION: Court Case. A tap-through mock trial with {name} as the defendant.
Write: case title, 3 charges (funny, harmless, from real habits in {facts}), 3 exhibits (label plus a 12-word description tied to a real memory), a witness (a real person or pet in {facts}, or "The Snacks") with a testimony (max 25 words), the judge's verdict (max 20 words) and a sentence (warm and silly, e.g. "a lifetime of hugs"). Never accuse of anything real or serious. Add "Not a real court."
OUTPUT: {"case":"","charges":[""],"exhibits":[{"label":"","desc":""}],"witness":{"who":"","line":""},"verdict":"","sentence":""}

{PREAMBLE}
SECTION: Wanted Poster. A vintage wanted poster for {name}.
Write: headline ("WANTED for crimes against ..."), alias (nickname or epithet), 4 crimes (max 8 words, affectionate, from {facts}), last_seen (max 8 words, a real place or habit), reward (max 8 words, something the giver truly offers: a hug, dinner) and return_to (the giver, "{from}"). Suggest a portrait treatment (sepia photo or silhouette). Friendly bounty only: no weapons, no danger.
OUTPUT: {"headline":"","alias":"","crimes":[""],"last_seen":"","reward":"","return_to":"","portrait":""}

{PREAMBLE}
SECTION: Fine Print. Scroll-to-accept terms and conditions for {name}'s friendship (or family membership).
Write 8 clauses (max 24 words each) titled like legal sections ("3.2 Punctuality"), each satirizing a real habit or fact in {facts}. One clause must be sincere ("7.1 We will always show up") to land the heart. Add a cheeky Privacy clause (max 20 words), an accept label, a decline label (the button dodges or comes back) and an after-accept line. It must be readable in 40 seconds.
OUTPUT: {"title":"","clauses":[{"n":"","title":"","text":""}],"accept":"","decline":"","after_accept":""}

{PREAMBLE}
SECTION: Owner's Manual. A product manual for {name}, model "{name} v{age}".
Write: in_box (3 real items from {facts}), getting_started (3 steps, max 14 words each), care (3 real preferences), troubleshooting (4 rows: symptom then fix, from real habits, e.g. "Won't start: coffee"), warnings (2, affectionate) and warranty (max 20 words, sincere: lifetime). Keep the voice of dry product documentation.
OUTPUT: {"model":"","in_box":[""],"getting_started":[""],"care":[""],"troubleshooting":[{"symptom":"","fix":""}],"warnings":[""],"warranty":""}

{PREAMBLE}
SECTION: Résumé & Endorsements. A professional-style profile for {name}.
Write: headline (max 10 words), 3 experience entries (title, org from a real place or hobby in {facts}, dates left blank if unknown, bullet max 15 words), 6 skills each with an endorsement count and 2 endorsers taken ONLY from names in {facts}, and 2 recommendations in the voice of real people in {facts}, kind and clearly labelled "dramatization".
OUTPUT: {"headline":"","experience":[{"title":"","org":"","bullet":""}],"skills":[{"name":"","endorsers":[""],"count":0}],"recommendations":[{"from":"","text":""}]}

{PREAMBLE}
SECTION: Group Chat Replay. An animated group chat where the friends plan {name}'s birthday and {name} joins at the end.
Use ONLY names in {facts} and {from}. Write 12 to 16 messages (max 14 words each) with sender, text and delay_ms. They reference real habits and phrases in {facts}, include one "left on read" beat and one running joke, and end with {name}'s reply using their real catchphrase ({phrase}) if there is one. Label the chat "Dramatization" in the header. No swearing, nothing mean.
OUTPUT: {"chat_name":"","messages":[{"from":"","text":"","delay_ms":0}],"final_reply":{"from":"","text":""}}

{PREAMBLE}
SECTION: Departure Board. A split-flap departure board where every row is about {name}.
Write a title ("Departures: {name}'s {age}th") and 8 rows: time (blank if unknown), dest (a phrase from {facts}), gate (a joke, max 3 characters) and status (ON TIME, DELAYED, BOARDING, CANCELLED or LEGENDARY). Include the classic gag row for a real habit. The last row is the only BOARDING row and points to the cake. Add a one-line announcement (max 14 words).
OUTPUT: {"title":"","rows":[{"time":"","dest":"","gate":"","status":""}],"announcement":""}

{PREAMBLE}
SECTION: Catch Game. The recipient moves a basket or character to catch falling items for 30 seconds.
Write: title (max 5 words), player (an object or pet from {facts}), 4 GOOD items from real obsessions (name plus a pixel-icon description; +1 each), 2 BAD items that are harmless jokes (name plus icon; -1 each), a golden item (worth 5), a win line at 15 or more (max 14 words) and a kind try-again line (max 14 words). Nobody loses.
OUTPUT: {"title":"","player":"","good":[{"name":"","icon":""}],"bad":[{"name":"","icon":""}],"golden":"","win":"","try_again":""}

{PREAMBLE}
SECTION: Tap Challenge. A big button counts taps with milestone messages and a confetti burst.
Choose the button label and what is being counted (a real habit, e.g. "Espresso Reps"). Write milestone messages for taps 1, 3, 5, 8, 10, 12, 15, 20 and 30 (max 10 words each, rising in silliness, referencing {facts}), a confetti line for tap 10, a warm secret at tap 50, and a stat label ("Reps", "Snacks", "Laps"). No body or fitness-shaming jokes.
OUTPUT: {"button":"","stat":"","milestones":{"1":"","3":"","5":"","8":"","10":"","12":"","15":"","20":"","30":""},"secret_50":""}

{PREAMBLE}
SECTION: Fill the Meter. Tapping fills a gauge that represents a real obsession (cups of coffee, laps, pages read).
Choose the gauge label, the unit and the number of steps (8 to 10). Write a reaction per step (max 8 words each, escalating), a "full" celebration line (max 14 words), a "reset" gag that empties the meter once (e.g. "It was decaf"), and a warm line after the last step (max 14 words). Avoid alcohol themes.
OUTPUT: {"gauge":"","unit":"","steps":[""],"full":"","reset_gag":"","warm":""}

{PREAMBLE}
SECTION: Memory Match. A card-flip pairs game with 6 pairs (8 for older players).
Write: title (max 5 words) and 6 pairs. Each pair: icon (a pixel-art description of a real thing in {facts}), label (max 3 words) and note (max 12 words, a tiny fact or joke from {facts}, shown when matched). Add a finish line (max 16 words). For under-9s use 6 pairs with bigger tiles and very short notes.
OUTPUT: {"title":"","pairs":[{"icon":"","label":"","note":""}],"finish":""}

{PREAMBLE}
SECTION: Perfect Timing. A marker slides back and forth and the recipient taps to stop it in the target zone. Three rounds, each faster.
Theme it on one real habit ({habit}): the marker (e.g. a cyclist), the target (e.g. "cafe door"), 3 round names, and short reactions for MISS, CLOSE and PERFECT (max 8 words each, funny), plus a final line (max 14 words) that is warm whatever the score.
OUTPUT: {"theme":"","marker":"","target":"","rounds":["","",""],"miss":"","close":"","perfect":"","final":""}

{PREAMBLE}
SECTION: Spin the Wheel. A prize wheel with 8 segments; every spin lands on something good.
Write a title (max 5 words) and 8 segments: label (max 4 words) plus a result (max 16 words). Mix 3 gifts the giver can truly offer ("Dinner on me"), 3 jokes from real facts ("10 minute grace period") and 2 warm messages. Mark one jackpot segment (always the same warm final message) that the wheel lands on at spin 3. Offer only things the giver can deliver.
OUTPUT: {"title":"","segments":[{"label":"","result":""}],"jackpot_index":0}

{PREAMBLE}
SECTION: Word Puzzle. Choose "crossword" (5x5 mini, 4 to 6 entries) or "wordsearch" (10x10).
Give 8 to 10 words (3 to 10 letters, A to Z only) drawn from {facts} (names, places, hobbies). For a crossword, add a clue for each (max 12 words, a joke or memory); for a word search, no clues. Add a hidden bonus word (their name or a warm 5-letter word) and the message revealed when everything is found. The generator lays out the grid: return only words and clues. Add a title (max 5 words).
OUTPUT: {"mode":"","title":"","words":[{"answer":"","clue":""}],"bonus":"","bonus_reveal":""}

{PREAMBLE}
SECTION: Quiz. A 6-question multiple-choice quiz about {name}, built only from real facts.
Write 6 questions (max 16 words). Each has 3 options: 1 correct (from {facts}), 1 plausible decoy and 1 absurd decoy. Add a reaction for right and wrong (max 10 words each). Question 6 is warm ("What did {from} say...?"). Add 3 result tiers (scores 0-2, 3-4, 5-6) with a title and a one-line verdict that lands warm at every level. Mark which fact id each question uses.
OUTPUT: {"title":"","questions":[{"q":"","options":["","",""],"correct":0,"fact_id":"","right":"","wrong":""}],"results":[{"min":0,"title":"","line":""}]}

{PREAMBLE}
SECTION: Identity Check. A fake "Prove you're {name}" verification with three challenges, then a verified stamp.
Write: title (max 6 words); grid (a prompt like "Select all squares with snacks", 9 tile labels from real objects in {facts}, and the correct tile indexes); checkbox (a label, and the gag that happens on click); question (a security question only {name} would answer, with the answer taken from {facts}, max 8 words); success copy (max 16 words); and a warm "verified human" stamp message. Do not imitate any real service.
OUTPUT: {"title":"","grid":{"prompt":"","tiles":[""],"correct":[0]},"checkbox":{"label":"","gag":""},"question":{"q":"","a":""},"success":"","stamp":""}

{PREAMBLE}
SECTION: Mad Libs. The recipient types words; the card writes a short story about {name}.
Write a 90 to 120 word story with 8 blanks ({noun}, {verb}, {adjective}, {place}, {food}, {number}, {animal}, {silly_word}). The fixed text carries real facts from {facts}; the blanks never contain facts. Give a prompt label for each blank, in story order. The final sentence is fixed and warm. Give the story a title. Keep it age-appropriate for {age}.
OUTPUT: {"title":"","blanks":[{"key":"","label":""}],"story":"text with {key} tokens","warm_end":""}

{PREAMBLE}
SECTION: The Year You Were Born. A page about the year {name} arrived.
INPUT: {birth_year} and {DATA_PACK} for that year (prices, top songs, films, gadgets, sports champions, world firsts). Use ONLY items in {DATA_PACK}; never recall from memory. Choose 8 items and write, for each: category, item and a one-line tie-back to {facts} or a time-travel joke (max 16 words). Add an opener ("The year {name} arrived") and a closing "Then you turned up" line. If no {DATA_PACK} is supplied, return {"skip":true}.
OUTPUT: {"year":0,"opener":"","items":[{"category":"","item":"","line":""}],"closing":""}

{PREAMBLE}
SECTION: Sing-Along Song. Original lyrics for a 60 to 90 second synthesized track, with the current line highlighted in time.
Choose a style (punk, sea shanty, lullaby, disco, country, light hip hop, power ballad) that matches {tone} and the person. Write 4 verses of 4 lines (max 9 words per line) and a 2-line chorus that includes {phrase} or the name. Rhyme AABB. Reference only real facts. No existing lyrics, artists or melodies: the tune is original. Also give bpm, mode (major or minor), a song title, a mixtape sleeve title, and an optional spoken tag.
OUTPUT: {"title":"","style":"","bpm":0,"mode":"","verses":[["x4"]],"chorus":["",""],"tag":""}

{PREAMBLE}
SECTION: Beat Pads. A 16-pad sampler where the recipient makes a beat from sounds tied to their world.
Name 8 pads (max 2 words, from {facts}) and give each a synth sound from: kick, snare, hat, clap, bell, blip, zap, bass, bark, tada. Write a starter loop (16 steps for 4 pads), a goal hint (max 10 words), a hidden combination (3 pads in order) that unlocks a warm message (max 16 words), and a title (max 5 words).
OUTPUT: {"title":"","pads":[{"label":"","sound":""}],"starter":[[0,1]],"hint":"","secret":{"combo":[0,1,2],"message":""}}

{PREAMBLE}
SECTION: Voice Notes. Real voice messages recorded by the giver and friends, shown as tapes.
You do NOT write the words spoken. Write: an intro line (max 16 words); and for each contributor, a recording prompt (max 25 words, given {relationship} and {facts}: e.g. "Tell {name} about the time..., 30 seconds, no planning"), a label for the tape (max 5 words, funny) and max_seconds. 3 to 6 notes, 90 seconds each at most.
OUTPUT: {"intro":"","notes":[{"contributor":"","prompt":"","label":"","max_seconds":0}]}

{PREAMBLE}
SECTION: Catchphrase Buttons. A soundboard: each big button plays one of {name}'s real phrases with a tiny animation.
Use ONLY phrases in {facts} (kind: phrase), plus up to 4 mash-ups (max 8 words) that remix them. 6 to 8 buttons: label, line (max 10 words), anim (shake, zoom, confetti, spin or bounce) and a colour. Add one hidden button (revealed after 5 taps) whose line begins with their phrase and ends with a kindness.
OUTPUT: {"buttons":[{"label":"","line":"","anim":"","color":""}],"secret":{"line":""}}

{PREAMBLE}
SECTION: The Letter. A short letter, in the giver's voice, that lands the real reason {from} adores {name}.
Write 90 to 140 words in first person, warm, specific, plain words. Structure: one line that calls back a joke from earlier in the card; 2 or 3 sentences on a real story or value from {facts}; one sentence that states the truth in plain words (e.g. "The snacks were never the point."); a simple sign-off. No cliches ("you mean the world"), no exclamation marks. Add a P.S. (max 14 words, light). Suggest a font style (handwriting, typewriter or marker).
OUTPUT: {"greeting":"","body":"","truth_line":"","signoff":"","ps":"","style":""}

{PREAMBLE}
SECTION: N Reasons. A counter runs up to {age} while reasons flick past; a few stop and glow.
Write 7 reasons (max 14 words each, from {facts}) numbered at spaced values (e.g. 1, 4, 9, 17, 25, 33, then {age} minus 1), and a final reason numbered {age} (max 20 words, the most sincere). Add a blur line (max 12 words) for the rest ("...and a few hundred more we ran out of room for"). Count-up duration is 6 seconds.
OUTPUT: {"reasons":[{"n":0,"text":""}],"blur":"","final":{"n":0,"text":""}}

{PREAMBLE}
SECTION: Coupon Book. 6 redeemable coupons the giver truly promises.
Write 6 coupons: title (max 5 words), fine_print (max 14 words, a joke) and tag (Free, Priority, Unlimited or One-time). At least 3 are sincere and doable ("One bike-shop trip, my treat"), 2 are jokes and 1 is a blank "Ask me anything". Add a redeem button label and a message shown after redeeming (max 12 words). Do NOT offer anything costly, romantic or hard to keep unless {facts} say it is welcome.
OUTPUT: {"coupons":[{"title":"","fine_print":"","tag":""}],"redeem_label":"","redeemed_line":""}

{PREAMBLE}
SECTION: Group Signature Wall. Each contributor adds a message, a doodle or a photo; the wall shows them as sticky notes.
Write: an invitation the giver sends to contributors (max 45 words: what to write, the deadline, friendly); 3 tap-to-use note starters ("The time {name}..."); a wall title (max 5 words); an empty-state line (max 12 words). Moderation rule to apply to every note: reject anything that mentions {avoid}, and rewrite mean jokes as neutral.
OUTPUT: {"invite":"","starters":["","",""],"title":"","empty_state":""}

{PREAMBLE}
SECTION: Fortune Cookie. The recipient taps to crack a cookie and read a fortune. Five cookies.
Write 5 fortunes (max 18 words each): 2 funny predictions from real habits ("You will arrive ten minutes late to your own party."), 2 sincere lines and 1 lucky-number line using {age} plus 3 other numbers. Fortune 5 is the real one from the giver's heart. Add a lucky item and a lucky colour. Fortunes are jokes: no predictions about health, money or relationships.
OUTPUT: {"fortunes":["x5"],"lucky_numbers":[0],"lucky_item":"","lucky_colour":""}

{PREAMBLE}
SECTION: Top 5 Countdown. A TV-style countdown reveals the "Top 5 things about {name}" from #5 to #1.
Write a list title (max 8 words), a host intro (max 14 words) and 5 entries: rank, title (max 12 words) and why (max 18 words), from {facts}. #5 and #4 are funny, #3 is a memory, #2 is a quirk we love, #1 is the sincere reason. Add a drumroll line before #1.
OUTPUT: {"title":"","intro":"","entries":[{"rank":5,"title":"","why":""}],"drumroll":""}

{PREAMBLE}
SECTION: Launch Sequence. A big red button starts a scripted countdown, then the payoff.
Choose a theme: deploy, rocket, cake_vault, confetti_cannon or time_machine (match {facts}). Write: the button label (max 4 words), 12 typed status lines (max 40 characters each; the middle ones turn real habits into tasks, e.g. "Loading punctuality... skipped"), a final GO line and a payoff message (max 16 words). The payoff triggers the finale: cake, confetti and a track.
OUTPUT: {"theme":"","button":"","lines":["x12"],"go":"","payoff":""}

{PREAMBLE}
SECTION: Candle Blowout. A cake with {age} candles (show at most 9, then "+N more") that the recipient blows out with the mic or taps out one by one.
Write: a cake description (max 8 words, tied to {facts}), 3 wish prompts (max 12 words each), a reaction for each candle going out (max 6 words), an optional trick-candle gag (only if {tone} allows) and the final greeting (max 16 words).
OUTPUT: {"cake":"","wish_prompts":["","",""],"candle_lines":[""],"trick_gag":"","final":""}

{PREAMBLE}
SECTION: Credits & Easter Egg. Rolling end credits with fake job titles and a hidden reboot.
Write 8 to 10 credit lines (role and name), with roles from real facts and names ONLY from {from} and real people in {facts}. Add a "Special thanks" line (a pet, the espresso machine), a fine-print line ("No punctuality was harmed"), an easter egg (where it hides, plus a warm secret line, max 20 words) and a sign-off ("Refresh to replay").
OUTPUT: {"credits":[{"role":"","name":""}],"thanks":"","fine_print":"","easter_egg":{"where":"","message":""},"signoff":""}

{PREAMBLE}
SECTION: Achievements Unlocked. Small badges pop up as the recipient explores the card.
